   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Text Classification Pipeline for Economic News Articles\n",
    "### Case Study — CO1, CO2, CO3\n",
    "\n",
    "**Task:** Classify news articles as **Relevant** or **Not Relevant** to the US economy, using the *Economic News Article Tone and Relevance* dataset (~8,000 articles: ~1,420 Relevant / ~6,571 Not Relevant).\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook is self-contained and runs top-to-bottom in Google Colab. It covers:\n",
    "1. Data preparation & pre-processing\n",
    "2. Bag-of-Words feature extraction (max_features = 40,000 / 5,000 / 1,000)\n",
    "3. Classification (Naive Bayes, Logistic Regression, LinearSVC) + confusion matrices\n",
    "4. Class imbalance analysis\n",
    "5. Model comparison\n",
    "6. Performance-improvement experiments\n",
    "7. Final consolidated analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Google Collab :** `[https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1nKoM-DZconKnxEaY1AeFDnAZca2bHF46?usp=sharing]`\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d6ffdead",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 0. Setup — install & import libraries"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "34dff5a1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Run once per Colab session\n",
    "!pip -q install scikit-learn pandas matplotlib seaborn nltk\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "70726861",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import re\n",
    "import string\n",
    "import json\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split, GridSearchCV\n",
    "from sklearn.feature_extraction.text import CountVectorizer\n",
    "from sklearn.naive_bayes import MultinomialNB\n",
    "from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n",
    "from sklearn.svm import LinearSVC\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import (accuracy_score, precision_score, recall_score,\n",
    "                              f1_score, confusion_matrix, classification_report)\n",
    "\n",
    "import nltk\n",
    "nltk.download('stopwords', quiet=True)\n",
    "from nltk.corpus import stopwords\n",
    "\n",
    "RANDOM_STATE = 42\n",
    "LABELS = [\"Relevant\", \"Not Relevant\"]\n",
    "STOPWORDS = set(stopwords.words(\"english\"))\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.set_style(\"whitegrid\")\n",
    "print(\"Libraries loaded.\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d584539f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Data Preparation and Pre-processing (2 marks)\n",
    "\n",
    "### 1.1 Download & load the dataset\n",
    "The dataset (`Full-Economic-News-DFE-839861.csv`, CrowdFlower / Figure Eight) is fetched directly from GitHub so the notebook runs standalone in Colab.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "fb21308c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Download the dataset (mirrors the original CrowdFlower/Figure Eight release)\n",
    "!wget -q -O economic_news.csv \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/practical-nlp/practical-nlp-code/master/Ch4/Data/Full-Economic-News-DFE-839861.csv\"\n",
    "\n",
    "df_raw = pd.read_csv(\"economic_news.csv\", encoding=\"latin-1\")\n",
    "print(\"Raw shape:\", df_raw.shape)\n",
    "df_raw.head(3)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a6e1db61",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Identify text and target/relevance columns, keep only usable rows\n",
    "df = df_raw[[\"text\", \"relevance\"]].dropna()\n",
    "df = df[df[\"relevance\"].isin([\"yes\", \"no\"])].reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "df[\"label\"] = df[\"relevance\"].map({\"yes\": \"Relevant\", \"no\": \"Not Relevant\"})\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Total usable articles: {len(df)}\")\n",
    "print(df[\"label\"].value_counts())\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3e0b3066",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1.2 Text pre-processing\\nLowercasing, punctuation/digit removal, stop-word removal, and whitespace/URL cleanup."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "73652712",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def preprocess_text(text: str) -> str:\n",
    "    text = str(text).lower()\n",
    "    text = re.sub(r\"http\\S+|www\\S+\", \" \", text)          # URLs\n",
    "    text = re.sub(r\"[^a-z\\s]\", \" \", text)                  # punctuation + digits\n",
    "    text = text.translate(str.maketrans(\"\", \"\", string.punctuation))\n",
    "    tokens = text.split()\n",
    "    tokens = [t for t in tokens if t not in STOPWORDS and len(t) > 2]\n",
    "    return \" \".join(tokens)\n",
    "\n",
    "df[\"clean_text\"] = df[\"text\"].apply(preprocess_text)\n",
    "df = df[df[\"clean_text\"].str.len() > 0].reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"RAW  :\", df[\"text\"].iloc[0][:150])\n",
    "print(\"CLEAN:\", df[\"clean_text\"].iloc[0][:150])\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c5825670",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1.3 Train / test split and class distribution"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7d52f6eb",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X = df[\"clean_text\"]\n",
    "y = df[\"label\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n",
    "    X, y, test_size=0.2, random_state=RANDOM_STATE, stratify=y\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Training instances: {len(X_train)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Testing instances : {len(X_test)}\")\n",
    "print(\"\\nTraining distribution:\\n\", y_train.value_counts())\n",
    "print(\"\\nTesting distribution:\\n\", y_test.value_counts())\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7345327b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(11, 4))\n",
    "\n",
    "overall = df[\"label\"].value_counts()\n",
    "axes[0].bar(overall.index, overall.values, color=[\"#4C72B0\", \"#DD8452\"])\n",
    "axes[0].set_title(f\"Overall Class Distribution (n={len(df)})\")\n",
    "for i, v in enumerate(overall.values):\n",
    "    axes[0].text(i, v + 50, str(v), ha=\"center\")\n",
    "\n",
    "x = np.arange(2)\n",
    "w = 0.35\n",
    "train_counts = [y_train.value_counts()[l] for l in LABELS[::-1]]\n",
    "test_counts = [y_test.value_counts()[l] for l in LABELS[::-1]]\n",
    "axes[1].bar(x - w/2, train_counts, w, label=\"Train\")\n",
    "axes[1].bar(x + w/2, test_counts, w, label=\"Test\")\n",
    "axes[1].set_xticks(x)\n",
    "axes[1].set_xticklabels(LABELS[::-1])\n",
    "axes[1].set_title(\"Train/Test Split Distribution\")\n",
    "axes[1].legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "996b94be",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Feature Extraction (1 mark)\n",
    "\n",
    "Convert pre-processed text into Bag-of-Words features with `CountVectorizer`, comparing `max_features` = 40,000 / 5,000 / 1,000.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "0dda176b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "feature_sizes = [40000, 5000, 1000]\n",
    "vocab_sizes = {}\n",
    "\n",
    "for max_feat in feature_sizes:\n",
    "    vec = CountVectorizer(max_features=max_feat)\n",
    "    Xtr = vec.fit_transform(X_train)\n",
    "    vocab_sizes[max_feat] = len(vec.vocabulary_)\n",
    "    print(f\"max_features={max_feat:>6}  ->  actual vocabulary size = {len(vec.vocabulary_):>6}  |  train matrix shape = {Xtr.shape}\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8ec67869",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Observation:** the cleaned corpus has ~35,600 unique tokens, so `max_features=40000` captures the *entire* vocabulary (no truncation). At 5,000 and 1,000, only the most frequent terms are kept."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ba17be33",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Classification (3 marks)\n",
    "\n",
    "Train and evaluate four configurations — Multinomial Naive Bayes, Logistic Regression, LinearSVC (default), and LinearSVC (`class_weight=\"balanced\"`) — at each of the three feature sizes. Metrics are computed for the **Relevant** class (the minority / class of interest).\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "0f2e916b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "classifiers = {\n",
    "    \"Multinomial Naive Bayes\": lambda: MultinomialNB(),\n",
    "    \"Logistic Regression\": lambda: LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000, random_state=RANDOM_STATE),\n",
    "    \"LinearSVC\": lambda: LinearSVC(random_state=RANDOM_STATE, max_iter=5000),\n",
    "    \"LinearSVC (balanced)\": lambda: LinearSVC(class_weight=\"balanced\", random_state=RANDOM_STATE, max_iter=5000),\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "all_results = []\n",
    "vectorizers = {}\n",
    "matrices = {}   # (max_feat, clf_name) -> (Xtr, Xte)\n",
    "\n",
    "for max_feat in feature_sizes:\n",
    "    vec = CountVectorizer(max_features=max_feat)\n",
    "    Xtr = vec.fit_transform(X_train)\n",
    "    Xte = vec.transform(X_test)\n",
    "    vectorizers[max_feat] = vec\n",
    "\n",
    "    for clf_name, clf_fn in classifiers.items():\n",
    "        clf = clf_fn()\n",
    "        clf.fit(Xtr, y_train)\n",
    "        preds = clf.predict(Xte)\n",
    "\n",
    "        acc = accuracy_score(y_test, preds)\n",
    "        prec = precision_score(y_test, preds, pos_label=\"Relevant\")\n",
    "        rec = recall_score(y_test, preds, pos_label=\"Relevant\")\n",
    "        f1 = f1_score(y_test, preds, pos_label=\"Relevant\")\n",
    "        cm = confusion_matrix(y_test, preds, labels=LABELS)\n",
    "\n",
    "        all_results.append({\n",
    "            \"max_features\": max_feat, \"classifier\": clf_name,\n",
    "            \"accuracy\": acc, \"precision\": prec, \"recall\": rec, \"f1\": f1,\n",
    "            \"confusion_matrix\": cm,\n",
    "        })\n",
    "\n",
    "results_df = pd.DataFrame(all_results)\n",
    "display_df = results_df.drop(columns=\"confusion_matrix\").copy()\n",
    "for c in [\"accuracy\", \"precision\", \"recall\", \"f1\"]:\n",
    "    display_df[c] = (display_df[c] * 100).round(2)\n",
    "display_df\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "65e76c64",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3.1 Confusion matrices (max_features = 5,000)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "16e98139",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 4, figsize=(20, 4.5))\n",
    "subset = results_df[results_df[\"max_features\"] == 5000]\n",
    "\n",
    "for ax, (_, row) in zip(axes, subset.iterrows()):\n",
    "    sns.heatmap(row[\"confusion_matrix\"], annot=True, fmt=\"d\", cmap=\"Blues\",\n",
    "                xticklabels=LABELS, yticklabels=LABELS, cbar=False, ax=ax)\n",
    "    ax.set_title(row[\"classifier\"], fontsize=11)\n",
    "    ax.set_xlabel(\"Predicted\")\n",
    "    ax.set_ylabel(\"Actual\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2df6eff0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3.2 Confusion matrices — all classifiers x all feature sizes"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "f26e3771",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(3, 4, figsize=(20, 13))\n",
    "\n",
    "for i, max_feat in enumerate(feature_sizes):\n",
    "    subset = results_df[results_df[\"max_features\"] == max_feat]\n",
    "    for j, (_, row) in enumerate(subset.iterrows()):\n",
    "        ax = axes[i, j]\n",
    "        sns.heatmap(row[\"confusion_matrix\"], annot=True, fmt=\"d\", cmap=\"Blues\",\n",
    "                    xticklabels=LABELS, yticklabels=LABELS, cbar=False, ax=ax)\n",
    "        ax.set_title(f'{row[\"classifier\"]}\\n(max_features={max_feat})', fontsize=10)\n",
    "        ax.set_xlabel(\"Predicted\")\n",
    "        ax.set_ylabel(\"Actual\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "4f25077d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# F1-score vs. feature size, across classifiers\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 5))\n",
    "for clf_name in results_df[\"classifier\"].unique():\n",
    "    sub = results_df[results_df[\"classifier\"] == clf_name].sort_values(\"max_features\")\n",
    "    ax.plot(sub[\"max_features\"].astype(str), sub[\"f1\"], marker=\"o\", label=clf_name)\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"max_features\")\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"F1-score (Relevant class)\")\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"F1-score vs. Feature Size Across Classifiers\")\n",
    "ax.legend(fontsize=9)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "35b28941",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Class Imbalance Analysis (1 mark)\n",
    "\n",
    "The dataset is imbalanced (~82% Not Relevant vs ~18% Relevant), so a trivial always-\"Not Relevant\" classifier would already score ~82% accuracy. Compare `LinearSVC()` (default) against `LinearSVC(class_weight=\"balanced\")` at each feature size.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b78f917d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "imbalance_cmp = results_df[results_df[\"classifier\"].isin([\"LinearSVC\", \"LinearSVC (balanced)\"])].copy()\n",
    "imbalance_display = imbalance_cmp.drop(columns=\"confusion_matrix\").copy()\n",
    "for c in [\"accuracy\", \"precision\", \"recall\", \"f1\"]:\n",
    "    imbalance_display[c] = (imbalance_display[c] * 100).round(2)\n",
    "imbalance_display.sort_values([\"max_features\", \"classifier\"])\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "f94ec19d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Confusion matrices: default vs balanced LinearSVC, max_features=1000\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(10, 4.5))\n",
    "pair = results_df[(results_df[\"max_features\"] == 1000) &\n",
    "                   (results_df[\"classifier\"].isin([\"LinearSVC\", \"LinearSVC (balanced)\"]))]\n",
    "\n",
    "for ax, (_, row) in zip(axes, pair.iterrows()):\n",
    "    sns.heatmap(row[\"confusion_matrix\"], annot=True, fmt=\"d\", cmap=\"Oranges\",\n",
    "                xticklabels=LABELS, yticklabels=LABELS, cbar=False, ax=ax)\n",
    "    ax.set_title(row[\"classifier\"] + \" (max_features=1000)\", fontsize=11)\n",
    "    ax.set_xlabel(\"Predicted\")\n",
    "    ax.set_ylabel(\"Actual\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0aa15f5e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Effect of balancing:** at every feature size, `class_weight=\"balanced\"` increases recall on the Relevant class — most dramatically at `max_features=1000` (recall roughly doubles). This comes at the cost of lower overall accuracy, because the balanced classifier now also flags more Not Relevant articles as Relevant (more false positives) in exchange for far fewer false negatives. Since missing a genuinely relevant article is normally costlier than a false alarm, class balancing is beneficial for this task — **accuracy alone is not an appropriate criterion** for this imbalanced problem.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2e7d86c0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Model Comparison (3 marks)\n",
    "\n",
    "Consolidate results across all classifiers and feature sizes to identify the best configuration by each metric.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1a1785f0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "best_acc = results_df.loc[results_df[\"accuracy\"].idxmax()]\n",
    "best_f1 = results_df.loc[results_df[\"f1\"].idxmax()]\n",
    "best_recall = results_df.loc[results_df[\"recall\"].idxmax()]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Best Accuracy : {best_acc['classifier']} @ max_features={best_acc['max_features']} -> {best_acc['accuracy']*100:.2f}%\")\n",
    "print(f\"Best F1-score : {best_f1['classifier']} @ max_features={best_f1['max_features']} -> {best_f1['f1']*100:.2f}%\")\n",
    "print(f\"Best Recall   : {best_recall['classifier']} @ max_features={best_recall['max_features']} -> {best_recall['recall']*100:.2f}%\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "adf46565",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Justification:** Naive Bayes consistently achieves the highest recall and F1-score on the Relevant class across all three feature sizes, even though its raw accuracy is lower than Logistic Regression or LinearSVC. Because this is a highly imbalanced, minority-class-of-interest problem, F1-score and recall are more meaningful selection criteria than accuracy. Naive Bayes' generative, per-word likelihood model is naturally less biased toward the majority class than the discriminative linear classifiers, which — without class weighting — tend to default toward predicting the majority \"Not Relevant\" label.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "622186b6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Code Modification and Performance Improvement (3 marks)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Baseline** for this section: `LinearSVC()` (default, unbalanced), unigrams, `max_features=5000` — the \"starting\" configuration from Section 3.\n",
    "Three improvement experiments are run and compared against it.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "12be3f68",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "baseline_row = results_df[(results_df[\"max_features\"] == 5000) & (results_df[\"classifier\"] == \"LinearSVC\")].iloc[0]\n",
    "baseline = {\n",
    "    \"name\": \"Baseline: LinearSVC (default), unigrams, max_features=5000\",\n",
    "    \"accuracy\": baseline_row[\"accuracy\"], \"precision\": baseline_row[\"precision\"],\n",
    "    \"recall\": baseline_row[\"recall\"], \"f1\": baseline_row[\"f1\"],\n",
    "}\n",
    "print(baseline)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e4a5e26a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 6.1 Experiment 1 — Unigram + Bigram features with balanced Logistic Regression"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "699b1538",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "vec1 = CountVectorizer(max_features=5000, ngram_range=(1, 2))\n",
    "Xtr1 = vec1.fit_transform(X_train)\n",
    "Xte1 = vec1.transform(X_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "clf1 = LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000, class_weight=\"balanced\", random_state=RANDOM_STATE)\n",
    "clf1.fit(Xtr1, y_train)\n",
    "preds1 = clf1.predict(Xte1)\n",
    "\n",
    "exp1 = {\n",
    "    \"name\": \"Exp 1: Unigram+Bigram (5000) + Logistic Regression (balanced)\",\n",
    "    \"accuracy\": accuracy_score(y_test, preds1),\n",
    "    \"precision\": precision_score(y_test, preds1, pos_label=\"Relevant\"),\n",
    "    \"recall\": recall_score(y_test, preds1, pos_label=\"Relevant\"),\n",
    "    \"f1\": f1_score(y_test, preds1, pos_label=\"Relevant\"),\n",
    "    \"cm\": confusion_matrix(y_test, preds1, labels=LABELS),\n",
    "}\n",
    "print(f\"Accuracy={exp1['accuracy']*100:.2f}%  Precision={exp1['precision']*100:.2f}%  Recall={exp1['recall']*100:.2f}%  F1={exp1['f1']*100:.2f}%\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0d56dd15",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 6.2 Experiment 2 — Hyperparameter-tuned, balanced LinearSVC (GridSearchCV)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "ebb62fc5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "vec2 = CountVectorizer(max_features=5000)\n",
    "Xtr2 = vec2.fit_transform(X_train)\n",
